# 📘 Pattern Extraction Rules from PDF Reports

## Purpose
These rules are extracted from the visual format of the PDFs:
- `ESTELITA - OBRAS 09-10-25 (2).pdf`
- `ESTELITA - FONOGRAMAS -09-10-25.pdf`

They define **how to segment and classify** blocks in raw tabular inputs.

---

## 🎯 Segmentation — Block Start Rules

A new record starts when:

- The line includes a **Title**, formatted as:
  - ALL CAPS (e.g. `A DANÇA DE NICODEMOS`)
  - Or Title Case with few punctuation marks
- Or the line contains:
  - ISWC: `T-XXX.XXX.XXX-X`
  - ISRC: `BR-XXX-YY-ZZZZZ`

---

## 🧠 Classification Within Blocks

| Field        | Pattern                                                                 |
|--------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **TITLE**    | All caps or title case + near "TÍTULO PRINCIPAL DA OBRA MUSICAL"       |
| **ARTIST**   | 2–4 capitalized words, may include connectors (de/da/do/e)             |
| **ASSOCIATION** | Contains UBC, ABRAMUS, SOCINPRO, SBACEM                              |
| **LABEL**    | Includes terms like `LTDA`, `EIRELI`, `EDITORA`, `PRODUÇÕES`, etc.     |
| **CODE**     | Valid ISWC or ISRC patterns                                             |
| **OTHER**    | Lines without match — ignored                                           |

---

## 🧪 Use in the Project

These patterns **are not parsed live from the PDF**, but used as **reference rules** when cleaning XLSX or DuckDB content.

The goal is to simulate what the PDF export was showing, using data fields (e.g., column headers like `titulo`, `autor`, `gravadora`) and format-based logic.

